{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 41, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Fair traveler thou seekest a journey to Japan's shore\nWhere ancient temples and gardens do abound in store\nA seven day sojourn shall be thy noble quest\nTo witness wonders of this mystic land at its best\n\nDay the First\nArise with morning sun and take thy leave from home\nFly to Tokyo's airport where thy journey doth begin to roam\nUpon arrival take a taxi to thy hotel's door\nAnd rest awhile to shake off weariness that doth implore\nIn evening stroll through Shinjuku's neon lights that shine\nAnd sample sushi at a humble restaurant of great design\n\nDay the Second\nRise with the dawn and take a train to Nikko's shrine\nWhere temples and pagodas do stand in all their splendor divine\nThe Toshogu Shrine a wonder to behold in its grandeur and might\nDoth tell the story of a great shogun's life and plight\nReturn to Tokyo in the evening and dine on tempura's sweet delight\n\nDay the Third\nVisit the Tsukiji Fish Market where the day's catch doth abound\nIn its stalls and shops thou shalt see the freshest seafood be found\nThence to the Asakusa Kannon Temple a place of great renown\nWhere ancient history and mystic legend doth entwine in a sacred crown\nIn evening stroll through the trendy Harajuku district's fashionable sway\n\nDay the Fourth\nTake a train to Kyoto the city of a thousand temples and more\nWhere ancient traditions and modern culture doth blend in a wondrous score\nVisit the Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousands of vermilion gates\nAnd walk the Philosopher's Path a scenic route that doth serenade\nIn evening dine on kaiseki a culinary art that doth delight\n\nDay the Fifth\nRise with the dawn and visit the Kinkaku-ji Temple of gold\nA symbol of Japan's rich history and a wonder to behold\nThence to the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove a place of serene and peaceful might\nWhere the gentle rustling of bamboo doth soothe the soul in the still 